 "narration": [
  "IGBC AP or LEED AP? If you're starting a green building career in India, here's the honest difference.",
  "IGBC AP comes from the Indian Green Building Council. It's built around Indian practice, and the exam isn't tied to a single rating system.",
  "Students and freshers can start with the IGBC AP Associate level.",
  "LEED AP comes from GBCI, the body that certifies LEED. It's a specialty credential, such as Building Design and Construction, that builds on the LEED Green Associate.",
  "So which one? Mostly Indian projects and clients: IGBC AP is a practical start. International firms or multinational clients: LEED carries more weight.",
  "Plenty of consultants end up holding both. Start with the one your next project needs.",
  "And check the current exam format and fees on the official websites before you book."
